iness the worst part was  the other founders didn't consider his  ideas when they were designing new  products so after a year he left so now  he has seven years of failing in the job  market and two failed startup businesses  under his bed  what would you do if you were in this  situation most people will be filled  with despair they feel like I've tried  everything I've tried every job I've  tried every business and it's not  working out what am I supposed to do so  he tapped back into his love of bicycles  and his dream of building the horseless  carriage he visited a local bicycle shop  got to know the two partners who founded  it and with them started a new business  his goal was to build the first  horseless carriage which would become  known as the automobile so after working  away for two years he finally had his  first prototype he was so excited  finally the first automobile and he set  up a live demonstration to show  everybody what his new invention could  do so in 1885 he set up the public  demonstration and unfortunately the  automobile was too difficult to control  and in front of everybody smashed into a  wall so here he is after two years of  research into developing and making this  prototype after two years before four  failed businesses after seven years  before failed jobs  everything's leading up to this moment  this day here it is is finally arrived  and it's a huge public failure for him  so what would you do that would you give  up and go do the same thing again and  get a job  it was Karl's dream so he had to keep  going it took him another two years of  developing and tinkering and modifying  before he had a product that was ready  for another big public demonstration in  1887 he had his new prototype ready for  demonstration at the Paris Expo it was a  success and in the summer of 1888 he  started taking orders and he had now the  first commercially available automobile  in history his dream of building a  horseless carriage had been realized and  he was on his way to building a  worldwide brand name this is a really  important lesson for you guys because if  you have a dream there's going to be  people who tell you not to do it you're  going to try a lot of things and you're  going to fail it might take years of  failing and failing and failing and  failing with no light anywhere at the  end of the tunnel  what keeps you motivated to keep going  you're going to want to quit and throw  in the towel multiple times the only  thing that keeps you excited is that  dream  it's at times in the rational belief  that you can make this dream a reality  and if you listen to your dream and  continue to take steps every day to move  towards it eventually you'll accomplish  it I maybe build a world recognizable  brand in the process to belief if you  guys like this video you want to see  more subscribe to the channel and let me  know what you think about this video by  leaving a comment below thank you so  much for watching and I'll see you soon  even your music isn't totally not secret  I look forward to them every they have  changed my life thank you  you
 

